  "notes": "TCL 58S571F (TCL Fire TV, S5 series, AFTDEC012E, codename ginza, MediaTek merak / mt5896), Fire OS 8 / Android 11\n(SDK 30), firmware RS8185.3885N, US. Same Fire OS 8 generation as hisense-fire-tv-aftcibfbd1/ and its notes apply\nhere; this list adds what this TCL set ships on top: OpApp, the KSO service, Luna, News, Gallery and System Status.\nThe same AFTDEC012E platform is also in examples/tcl-43s450f-ca/ (the S4 sibling) and examples/amazon-fire-tv-aftdec012e/.\n\nFIRE OS: DEBLOAT ONLY. com.amazon.tv.launcher keeps Home and also owns the full Settings grid on this firmware\n(MainSettingsActivity), so it must stay enabled. Live TV app: com.amazon.tv.livetv.\n\nApply:  TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/tcl-58s571f-fire-tv/debloat.txt\nUndo:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/tcl-58s571f-fire-tv/debloat.txt com.amazon.tv.launcher\nEverything is DISABLED for user 0, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nLived with since 2026-10-20 (the last group since 2026-10-21), through several reboots: Netflix, YouTube\n(SmartTube), Spotify, Stremio, AirPlay from an iPhone and a Mac, and Settings all work.\nEvery package stayed disabled across reboots.\n\nFire OS 8 notes (as on the Hisense):\n- com.amazon.vizzini (Alexa voice) comes back at every boot, so it is not listed. Setting secure voice_disabled=1\nturns voice off, but Fire OS resets it at boot too.\n- com.amazon.ftvads.deeplinking and com.amazon.device.crashmanager are protected (pm disable-user is refused).\n- com.amazon.device.telemetry.emitter disables, but its native emitter keeps running outside ActivityManager.\n\nKept on purpose: AirPlay, Miracast, Live TV, OTA updates, Silk, Quick Settings, profile picker, and the Appstore\n(app updates; the remote's branded buttons, Prime Video and the TV maker's app, are launched through it).\nPersonal choices are marked below.\nAds, shopping and content recognition",
